course: dictionary
lesson: 3623
title: Finance: the world of money
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Finance is a word about money. It means the way money is managed, borrowed and spent, especially by governments, banks and businesses. «Her dad works in finance in London and is hardly ever home before she's asleep.» The clue is works in: finance is a kind of work, the work of looking after money.
explain: Finance can also mean money that pays for something, such as a project or a purchase. As a verb, to finance something means to provide the money for it. Ask yourself: what is being paid for here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases have a special meaning. Buying a car «on finance» does not mean buying it with a finance; it means borrowing money and paying it back in parts. When a word sits in a phrase, the other words in that phrase tell you what it means.
fact: Finance means the management of money, especially by governments, banks and businesses.
fact: Finance can also mean money used to pay for a project or a purchase.
fact: As a verb, «to finance» something means to provide the money for it.
fact: «On finance» means buying something by borrowing money and paying it back in parts.
fact: A minister of finance is the person in charge of a government's money.
exercise: «Her dad works in finance in London and is hardly ever home before she's asleep.» What does finance mean here? | Being tired at bedtime | *The management of money, such as the work of banks and businesses | A kind of sports car | A type of city in London
exercise: Lily says she will buy a bike «on finance». What does that mean? | Paying for the bike in one go with coins | Painting the bike a new colour | *Borrowing money and paying it back in parts | Riding the bike very fast
exercise: The school wants to finance a new library. What does finance mean here? | To paint the walls of it | *To provide the money for it | To close it for the summer | To read every book in it
test: Which phrase is about managing your own money? | a personal diary | a personal best | *personal finance | a personal trainer
test: Which of these describes a government's finance? | How many people live there | Which sports its people play | *How it manages and spends its money | How tall its buildings are
exam: Finance can be a noun or a verb. Which sentence uses it as a verb? | Her finance job is in London | The finance books were on the shelf | *The bank agreed to finance the new bridge | The finance team went home early
